url: "https://github.com/RascalZ/REO"
abstract: "Research software comparing expression, within-sample ranks and relative-expression gene pairs with tissue references in cancer-cell-line drug-response prediction. The prepared v0.1.0 assets retain 64 frozen models, zero molecular solutions and minimal identity/fold metadata. The study did not establish an average REO predictive advantage. The software DOI has been reserved; registration and release publication are pending. No paper DOI is claimed. Code uses MIT, while author-owned model and derived assets have a separate CC BY 4.0 grant; third-party data and identifiers are not relicensed."
keywords:
  - pharmacogenomics
  - relative expression ordering
  - drug response prediction
  - reproducible research
